[SPEAKER_00]: It's just too much pressure.

345
00:29:13,097 --> 00:29:14,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I was careless.

346
00:29:14,078 --> 00:29:15,760
[SPEAKER_00]: I still don't know to what extent and how.

347
00:29:17,441 --> 00:29:19,182
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, well, go for a walk.

348
00:29:19,563 --> 00:29:21,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, technically, it's acting out.

349
00:29:22,105 --> 00:29:27,990
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not acting out on the level of fully distracting yourself with sense desires or winding yourself up with ill will and so on.

350
00:29:29,307 --> 00:29:36,130
[SPEAKER_00]: Because those kind of neutral acting-outs, or not as unwholesome acting-outs, won't make you drift too far away.

351
00:29:36,710 --> 00:29:38,491
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, then, you can recompose better.

352
00:29:38,531 --> 00:29:51,937
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all that... the simile in that sutra, it would have said, like, even if a monk, having gone to the forest, he's not making any effort, he's just sleeping all day, and having sensual thoughts all day long, and just not...

353
00:29:52,337 --> 00:29:57,379
[SPEAKER_00]: Nevertheless, he's in a more suitable environment, his mind will eventually calm down and compose.

354
00:29:58,943 --> 00:30:12,550
[SPEAKER_00]: Consequently, you have a monk in the middle of the village who is not sleeping, who is very diligent, who is not having lustful thoughts, but he's in the unsuitable environment with constant exposure to sight, sound, smell, taste, touches, so his mind will lose composure.

355
00:30:15,743 --> 00:30:26,839
[SPEAKER_03]: I think there's also there's also just an aspect that, you know, it's not that I need to kind of clarify these things more so that there will be no pressure to act out.

356
00:30:26,859 --> 00:30:27,139
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, yeah.

357
00:30:27,440 --> 00:30:29,923
[SPEAKER_03]: It's so, like, the whole point is that

358
00:30:30,404 --> 00:30:40,292
[SPEAKER_03]: You know, you have to start by not acting out in the face of everything that's... oh, I must... but I must... there is this pressure, but I don't act out of that pressure.

359
00:30:41,193 --> 00:30:49,059
[SPEAKER_03]: So, like, regardless of it... and that's how you would actually build up further clarity, and that would then make that pressure diminish in future.

360
00:30:50,901 --> 00:30:56,565
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, it's going to the village or the city or as he's traveling around.

361
00:30:57,666 --> 00:30:59,608
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, it's these gradual

362
00:31:01,598 --> 00:31:06,040
[SPEAKER_01]: Distractions, gradual... Erosions.

